  "assumptions": [
    "A single store/location is assumed; if multiple locations are needed later, add a locations table and a location_id column to stock_levels (with unique(product_id, location_id)) and stock_movements.",
    "All primary keys are uuid except stock_movements.id, which is bigint identity because of its high write volume; every table has exactly one single-column primary key, so junction tables use a surrogate id plus a composite UNIQUE index on the two foreign keys.",
    "Composite unique constraints and composite indexes are expressed in the indexes arrays as UNIQUE(col_a, col_b) or (col_a, col_b).",
    "Roles are many-to-many with users through user_roles, and permissions are many-to-many with roles through role_permissions, to support role-based access control; role-to-permission enforcement is done in the Node.js API.",
    "Supplier users are optional, read-only accounts linked to a supplier via users.supplier_id; access limits are enforced by the supplier role's permissions.",
    "Passwords are stored only as salted hashes in users.password_hash.",
    "stock_levels.quantity_on_hand is the live source of truth and is updated in the same database transaction as an insert into stock_movements; the version column supports optimistic locking for concurrent devices.",
    "Real-time propagation to clients uses WebSockets driven by application events or PostgreSQL LISTEN/NOTIFY on stock_levels changes, so no extra table is needed.",
    "stock_movements is append-only; rows are never updated or deleted, and foreign keys use RESTRICT to preserve audit history (the 30-day backup retention is handled at the infrastructure level).",
    "Low-stock alerts are created by the application or a database trigger when quantity_on_hand drops below reorder_threshold; suggested_reorder_quantity is copied from stock_levels.reorder_quantity at alert time.",
    "Unknown barcodes create a new products row plus a product_barcodes row; barcode values are globally unique.",
    "Monetary values use decimal(12,2); the sale price is snapshotted in sale_items.unit_price.",
    "Reports are computed from sales, sale_items, stock_levels, products and stock_movements; report_exports only logs requests and generated CSV files.",
    "Timestamps are stored in UTC."
  ]
}